target: internal/report/post.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestFindPRDistinguishesTheThreeCauses'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    this is the defect the whole slice exists to fix, reintroduced. pr-report.py branches on `rc != 0 or not num` and prints "no PR yet", which asserts the first of three causes and discards the only stream that says which. On this machine gh has already failed with a keychain TLS error while `git push` worked, so the unfixable branch is the reachable one and its advice ("make a PR") cannot help. Folding a non-zero exit back into NoPR restores exactly that conflation.
--- old
	case r.Code != 0:
		return Probe{State: GhFailed, Detail: firstLine(r.Err)}
--- new
	case r.Code != 0:
		return Probe{State: NoPR, Detail: firstLine(r.Err)}
